1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:05,579
Our cell-free reaction answers an AHL
signal by making sfGFP.

2
00:00:05,579 --> 00:00:10,202
Reading that answer normally means a
benchtop plate reader.

3
00:00:12,400 --> 00:00:17,421
A shared reader is booked, scheduled, and
in someone else's building.

4
00:00:17,421 --> 00:00:18,876
So we built our own.

5
00:00:18,876 --> 00:00:21,932
Cheap enough to sit next to the incubator,

6
00:00:21,932 --> 00:00:25,061
and open enough that anyone can rebuild
it.

7
00:00:26,800 --> 00:00:29,869
This is CAPTURE-Screen: a research-use,

8
00:00:29,869 --> 00:00:33,803
single-cuvette, ninety-degree fluorescence
reader.

9
00:00:33,803 --> 00:00:35,456
Here is how it works.

10
00:00:38,200 --> 00:00:41,100
It starts with one blue LED, a Cree part,

11
00:00:41,100 --> 00:00:44,211
nominal four hundred and seventy
nanometres.

12
00:00:44,211 --> 00:00:47,535
sfGFP takes in blue light and gives back
green.

13
00:00:47,535 --> 00:00:51,425
Our benchmark plate reader excites at four
eighty-five.

14
00:00:51,425 --> 00:00:54,183
Four seventy is deliberately different,

15
00:00:54,183 --> 00:00:57,012
and that difference is something we will

16
00:00:57,012 --> 00:00:59,699
have to characterise, not assume away.

17
00:01:00,600 --> 00:01:02,420
Here is the central idea.

18
00:01:02,420 --> 00:01:05,770
The excitation beam is overwhelmingly
brighter

19
00:01:05,770 --> 00:01:08,901
than the fluorescence we are trying to
see.

20
00:01:08,901 --> 00:01:12,105
So the detector does not look down the
beam.

21
00:01:12,105 --> 00:01:14,872
It looks across it, at ninety degrees.

22
00:01:14,872 --> 00:01:19,460
On that axis it sees the sample, and
almost none of the source.

23
00:01:20,600 --> 00:01:24,140
Before the sample, two aperture stops trim
the beam.

24
00:01:24,140 --> 00:01:26,727
After it, whatever the sample does not

25
00:01:26,727 --> 00:01:29,313
absorb runs into an angled wedge trap,

26
00:01:29,313 --> 00:01:33,125
slanted so that light is deflected rather
than returned.

27
00:01:33,125 --> 00:01:36,257
The far side of the axis belongs to that
trap,

28
00:01:36,257 --> 00:01:41,226
which is what makes this a fluorescence
geometry, not a transmission one.

29
00:01:42,800 --> 00:01:45,831
The sample sits in an Eppendorf UVette,

30
00:01:45,831 --> 00:01:49,095
in one fixed orientation we call ORIENT-A.

31
00:01:49,095 --> 00:01:53,214
The excitation crosses the short
two-millimetre path.

32
00:01:53,214 --> 00:01:56,945
The detector looks along the
ten-millimetre one.

33
00:01:56,945 --> 00:01:58,810
Two hundred microlitres.

34
00:02:00,200 --> 00:02:02,185
The detector is an AS7341,

35
00:02:02,185 --> 00:02:07,760
a spectral sensor with separate colour
channels, not a single photodiode.

36
00:02:07,760 --> 00:02:12,876
That lets us watch the excitation band and
the emission band apart,

37
00:02:12,876 --> 00:02:15,701
and measure the leakage between them.

38
00:02:15,701 --> 00:02:21,275
The slot in front of it holds the emission
filter, and is currently open.

39
00:02:22,200 --> 00:02:24,228
A reading is a timed window.

40
00:02:24,228 --> 00:02:27,921
The LED comes on, a hundred milliseconds
to settle,

41
00:02:27,921 --> 00:02:31,831
then four hundred and fifty-two to read
every channel.

42
00:02:31,831 --> 00:02:35,379
About five hundred and fifty milliseconds
in all,

43
00:02:35,379 --> 00:02:37,769
inside a one-second hard timeout.

44
00:02:37,769 --> 00:02:42,983
That window repeats once an hour, for six
hours at thirty-seven degrees.

45
00:02:44,600 --> 00:02:47,114
This is what the detector reads.

46
00:02:47,114 --> 00:02:51,828
With a scatterer in the sample seat, it
sees the excitation.

47
00:02:51,828 --> 00:02:56,071
Lid closed and the room lit, every channel
reads zero.

48
00:02:56,071 --> 00:02:59,214
LED on, nothing in the seat, still zero.

49
00:03:00,300 --> 00:03:05,686
So, precisely: CAPTURE-Screen reads
relative biosensor fluorescence,

50
00:03:05,686 --> 00:03:08,141
and flags optical interference.

51
00:03:12,600 --> 00:03:13,762
CAPTURE-Screen.

52
00:03:13,762 --> 00:03:17,558
A ninety-degree fluorescence reader we can
build,

53
00:03:17,558 --> 00:03:20,812
explain, and hand to anyone who needs one.

